    <node id="Butter">
      <data key="d0">Butter</data>
      <data key="d1">item</data>
      <data key="d2">"A rectangular piece of butter that is pale yellow in color."&lt;SEP&gt;Butter is a dairy product commonly used in cooking and baking, characterized by its pale yellow color and rectangular block shape. This versatile ingredient plays a significant role in enhancing the flavor and texture of a variety of culinary applications. Its primary uses include food preparation, where it serves to enrich dishes with its creamy consistency and rich taste.&lt;SEP&gt;"A small rectangular piece of pale yellow butter, unwrapped and ready for use."</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be sliced;"Can be spread;"N/A";"can be spread;"slice;"spread;"spreading;can be melted;cooking";melted;melting;melts;spread;use in cooking";used as an ingredient in recipes.";used in cooking recipes";used in cooking"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"Should be stored in a refrigerator after opening to maintain freshness";"keep refrigerated for freshness";"stored in a refrigerator after opening to maintain freshness"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">Butter is primarily situated near the center-right of the countertop, positioned close to the robotic arm. It is described as being in the center of the visible countertop area, specifically located below the robotic arm and above and to the right of a strawberry. Although there is a reference to the left side of the countertop, this description seems inconsistent with the overall positioning of butter and may pertain to a different context or arrangement. Thus, the coherent conclusion is that butter is predominantly found at the center-right of the countertop, maintaining proximity to the robotic arm.</data>
      <data key="d7">Butter is a dairy product commonly used in cooking and is described as rectangular in shape.&lt;SEP&gt;Butter is a pale yellow rectangular block, typically flat in shape, and is commonly used as both a cooking ingredient and a spread. It plays a significant role in culinary applications, enhancing flavor and texture in a variety of dishes. Positioned slightly to the left of the robotic arm's path on the kitchen countertop, it is also noted to be close to a strawberry, highlighting its importance in the cooking context. Butter is frequently found on kitchen countertops, serving as one of the key objects in food preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;Butter is presented as a rectangular slice of pale yellow color, positioned at the center of the countertop, ready for culinary use.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-61e0642e7493eaadc2d0ef8540a842ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c3bd83c5c76549d80af5d2102523481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54db96677933eae2def56d385069570f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc62d13e4271cfab3b042fbaf82ff07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83791e02fffc409681757eddcca76382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2663373a7c15d583525613b528aaf782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd7a3f830c9003a2fcb1b91e91ae47a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191e598f72ba5bb9098d142aa877c30b</data>
