    <node id="Sink">
      <data key="d0">Sink</data>
      <data key="d1">receptacle</data>
      <data key="d2">"A sink is a bowl or basin with a drain, often made of materials like ceramic, stainless steel, or plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;The sink is a vital plumbing fixture commonly found in kitchens and bathrooms, designed primarily for washing dishes, food, and hands. It consists of a basin that holds water, a faucet for water supply, and a drain for disposing of wastewater. Typically constructed from materials such as stainless steel or gray metal, sinks can vary in design but are often rectangular in shape and embedded in kitchen countertops. They play a crucial role in daily kitchen activities, serving as indispensable components for cleaning and food preparation. Additionally, the sink significantly contributes to maintaining hygiene and efficiency within the home.</data>
