      <data key="d7">Center of the countertop, slightly right of center. A wrench is a standard tool for household tasks, characterized by its shiny metallic surface and adjustable mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wrench is a metallic tool specifically designed for gripping and turning various sizes of nuts and bolts, essential for tasks involving fastening and loosening. In the kitchen, two types of wrenches are present: an open-ended wrench and an adjustable metallic wrench. The open-ended wrench is located on the left side of the kitchen counter, while the adjustable wrench lies flat on the countertop, closer to the sink. Both wrenches serve the same purpose and are positioned strategically on the countertop, making them conveniently accessible for any necessary adjustments. Together, they enhance the kitchen's functionality by aiding in the manipulation of nuts and bolts.&lt;SEP&gt;The metallic, darker-colored wrench is lying on the counter.</data>
