    <node id="Hammer">
      <data key="d0">Hammer</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">The hammer is a common and versatile hand tool that features a metallic head designed for driving nails into wood and other materials. It typically has a sturdy wooden handle that provides leverage and comfort during use. The design of the hammer includes a flat striking surface on its head, making it effective for various applications such as driving nails, fitting parts together, and breaking objects apart. Many hammers also incorporate a claw for efficient nail removal, further enhancing their utility. Known for its heavy head and long handle, the hammer is an essential tool in the toolkit of both professionals and DIY enthusiasts, underscoring its significance in construction, woodworking, and repair tasks. The hammer is fundamentally characterized by its tool design, which consists of a wooden handle and a metal head oriented diagonally for optimal striking capability.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be used for driving nails;"Can be used to drive nails;"Can be used to hammer nails;"Can be used to hit nails;"N/A";"can be used to drive nails;"can drive nails;"can pound;"hammer;"pick up;"strike;"strike nails;apply force";be held";be used to break objects;break objects;break objects";break things;drive nails;for demolition";interact";perform tasks requiring impact";pull nails;pulling nails;remove nails;remove nails (using the claw)";remove nails";shape materials";strike";striking surfaces";use;used in construction";used in construction."</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"Should not be used for demolition without safety gear;"Should not be used with excessive force on fragile materials";"keep_away_from_children";"not to be used on fragile objects;Caution when using around others.";caution when using around others";requires proper grip during use"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"Not recently used"</data>
      <data key="d6">"On the kitchen countertop (foreground); located slightly to the right of the green pear, handle pointing towards the bottom right."&lt;SEP&gt;"Right side of the counter;to the right of the pear"&lt;SEP&gt;The hammer is positioned on the countertop, specifically towards the center-right area. It is located right of a pear on the tabletop, with its handle pointing towards the bottom right. The head of the hammer is oriented upwards to the left while also being directed towards the right edge of the tabletop. This arrangement highlights the hammer's relationship with the nearby pear and provides a clear understanding of its placement on the counter.</data>
      <data key="d7">The hammer is a versatile handheld tool commonly used in construction and repairs, characterized by its metallic head and wooden handle. Specifically, it is identified as a claw hammer, which is designed for driving nails into various materials or breaking apart objects. In the context described, the hammer rests prominently at the center of a kitchen countertop, lying flat with its head pointed to the left and leaning slightly towards the lower left. This positioning makes it easily accessible, especially in relation to a nearby robotic arm, highlighting its practical use in a domestic environment.

The hammer is depicted beside a pear, further contributing to the everyday atmosphere of the kitchen setting. It is shown in an inactive state, symbolizing its role within the household and emphasizing its significance as a commonly used tool in home repair activities. Overall, the hammer serves as a functional item, notable for its claw design and integration into daily life, resting on the dark surface of the countertop alongside other household items.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-4ea0fff769b2e979e46cfd9106d4e1d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-842e2fbd96c01331a0e8b984f377b9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49dd2520a0dddbb4dcaa4dd60231f9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3bc1c91eadc47a11af404b983abb2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6fd8274a2d1232f9f77a0ea15e523e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f51a50808e472c1e342033e522e690&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4b6af94a6822cfe2dcbf1cfd9ea301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b6a597b9f445063e4005e101216236e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43c0038cb33aa953ea92fe00f539c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d89b523e359142053ba13f77d063f7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d801d05e69f4776674c9eeff32e1415c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c373a33b7f40d867bb7889415b47e8ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a33ad67667853c31418ab82889e1e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b12ac4b5e7ef4ee723211268193b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88d09cfcfcedc2adcc16d0314fe78275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f47b87b4b95fbe187651b52c3814eca</data>
