    <node id="Task Request">
      <data key="d0">Task Request</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"A request for performing a specific task."&lt;SEP&gt;A Task Request is an event that signifies a formal appeal for a specific action or task to be completed by an embodied agent. It encompasses requests for actions such as navigating to the refrigerator and performing observations, as well as tasks that involve object movement. Fundamentally, a Task Request focuses on engaging an agent in the execution of designated tasks, highlighting the interactive nature of the request. Overall, it represents a structured way to solicit particular actions from agents in a given context.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"perform task"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">A Task Request is an event type that signifies a need for observation or interaction with the environment, particularly in a kitchen setting. It serves as the initial trigger for actions performed by an embodied agent, guiding it towards a specific goal for interaction. For instance, a Task Request may entail navigating to the refrigerator to observe its contents, indicating a directed action that facilitates engagement with the kitchen environment. Additionally, a specific task has been initiated to move a pear item from one location to another, specifically to a sofa. Overall, the Task Request outlines the goal for the agent, detailing the necessary actions to navigate and observe within the kitchen environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The task request involves asking someone to close the open refrigerator door while ensuring access is unobstructed.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-fd7a3f830c9003a2fcb1b91e91ae47a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53daedf4d04d6753bedcb7a46e631c8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31e979835f2804ff8d1ce116dbce00c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d938391f0c5ac3146df4cf04a3a65025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6a9da891ede12376a00cfbf3a48e356&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f141569c90d0dc3f466444b6898c4311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2663373a7c15d583525613b528aaf782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512c99ba00abd1351acdffc5f28ef60b</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d10">1772546085</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Perception Update">
      <data key="d0">Perception Update</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"A specific event type focusing on the observation of the environment by an agent."&lt;SEP&gt;The Perception Update refers to an event that signifies the process of updating or altering perceptions based on observations. It involves the enhancement of awareness regarding the environment and the state of objects within it. This update is crucial for understanding and adapting one's viewpoint to align with new information acquired from the surrounding context. It encompasses observations made about the environment, reflecting the results of interactions that lead to a more informed perspective. Overall, the Perception Update emphasizes the importance of revising perceptions in response to updated environmental observations.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"observe environment"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">Perception Update indicates an observation event where the embodied agent analyzes the kitchen counter and its surroundings.&lt;SEP&gt;Perception Update refers to the comprehensive process through which an agent, such as an embodied robot, assesses its environment following navigation to specific locations, such as the kitchen counter or refrigerator. This event type signifies changes in the agent's understanding or awareness based on new observations and insights gathered during its interaction with the surroundings. Perception Updates involve recording initial environmental contexts and the statuses of specific objects nearby, reflecting the dynamic nature of the agent's awareness.

During this process, the agent observes its surroundings, interprets the information collected, and updates its comprehension accordingly. For instance, upon examining the interior of a refrigerator, the agent might note the absence of visible items, indicating a lack of identifiable features in that environment. This continuous updating of perceptual information is crucial for effective navigation tasks, allowing the agent to adapt its actions based on real-time assessments of its interactions with the environment.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-fd7a3f830c9003a2fcb1b91e91ae47a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53daedf4d04d6753bedcb7a46e631c8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31e979835f2804ff8d1ce116dbce00c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88d09cfcfcedc2adcc16d0314fe78275&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61e0642e7493eaadc2d0ef8540a842ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6a9da891ede12376a00cfbf3a48e356&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2663373a7c15d583525613b528aaf782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512c99ba00abd1351acdffc5f28ef60b</data>
