    <node id="Table">
      <data key="d0">Table</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">"A wooden table that serves as a central piece in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;A table is a piece of furniture characterized by a flat surface supported by one or more legs. It serves a variety of purposes, including activities such as eating, working, and displaying items. Commonly found in many settings, tables are essential for providing surfaces conducive to various activities. Additionally, some tables may be specifically designed as dark-colored furniture pieces used for displaying items or facilitating various activities. Overall, tables are flat-topped furniture items that play a crucial role in everyday life, supporting various objects and enabling different tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"Support items;"Support objects;"holding decorative items;"holds decorative items, food, or for dining";"navigate";"place items;"provides a surface for placement;"suitable for placing objects";"support;dining";eat";hold items";place";provide a surface";serve food;serving food;supports objects";work</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"may be obscured by other objects";"obscured by other objects";"should be maintained and kept clean"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The table is strategically positioned on the left side of the room, establishing its global position within the space. Locally, it is partially obscured by a robotic arm, indicating that it has a specific role within the arrangement of the room's layout. Additional descriptions provided do not contribute any further relevant information about the table.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Table is a central, dark-colored wooden structure located in an indoor setting, essential for various tasks and activities. It serves as the primary surface in the living space, where it facilitates interaction with a variety of objects, including plates, electronic devices, and decorative items such as a Decorative Bowl, a Small Blue Figurine, and a Yellow Apple. Positioned slightly to the right and behind the Large Round Object, the Table enhances the organization's overall aesthetic of the room. While its primary functions include holding assorted items and providing a flat surface for activities, its visibility may occasionally be limited by surrounding objects. Overall, the Table plays a crucial role in the arrangement and functionality of the living space, embodying both practical and decorative elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The Table is a wooden furniture piece positioned in the central area of the Indoor Environment.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-4efe4535ba7fd9b92fec1ad1e7648658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50ed04d922981d0130e000af0033b0c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff19d1455befb4bd03990a913dbb67f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac88e7624d72a183b4aa96fb7a5fd8cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd46b2147100e03f5fba63a01ed56378&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddbbb4c723348e17ec00fda3f50df18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97b6ebfa7e0b37e0577457d045a55bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b9e0b05991de9937fe35bfd38dcb802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-babdc4e6440123cf0378b9adab2b9736</data>
