    <node id="Plate">
      <data key="d0">Plate</data>
      <data key="d1">object</data>
      <data key="d2">"A flat dish typically used for serving or eating food; can be made from various materials like ceramic, glass, or plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;A plate is a flat dish typically used for serving or eating food, commonly circular in shape and often featuring a raised edge. Plates can be made from various materials, including ceramic and metal. They are designed to hold food and can be stacked for storage. Additionally, some plates have a reflective surface, enhancing their aesthetic appeal. Overall, plates serve as essential kitchenware items for both functional and decorative purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be filled with food;"Fragile if made of ceramic/glass;"holds food items;"interact;can be heavy;can be used for serving";held;observe";should be washed after use.";stacked;used for serving."</data>
      <data key="d4">"Fragile if made of ceramic/glass;"N/A";can be heavy;should be washed after use."</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">The entity, Plate, is referenced multiple times in the provided descriptions. The descriptions indicate that the Plate is located on the table, specifically on the left side of the table. While some descriptions contain "N/A," the key information consistently points to its position on the table. Therefore, the comprehensive description is that the Plate is situated on the left side of the table.</data>
      <data key="d7">A plate is a flat dish that serves the purpose of holding food. It is generally circular, flat, with a raised edge to contain food, and is commonly made from materials such as ceramic, glass, or plastic.&lt;SEP&gt;A plate is a round dish commonly found in dining settings, primarily used to hold and serve food. It is typically located on the table, and its material—often ceramic or metal—can impact its durability and functionality. The plate is reflective and is usually positioned on the left side of the table, making it a standard component of tableware.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-bccc7a95bec699180dde3a3987d59e0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61d59281ea4939e6692ff1c48515ab5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4efe4535ba7fd9b92fec1ad1e7648658</data>
