      <data key="d6">"typically located in the kitchen;under the countertop;adjacent to the stove"</data>
      <data key="d7">A kitchen sink serves as a receptacle that holds water and is essential for various kitchen functions, constructed from materials like stainless steel, ceramic, or composite, and typically includes a basin and faucet.&lt;SEP&gt;The Kitchen Sink is a gray rectangular basin situated centrally within the kitchen environment. It serves multiple purposes, primarily functioning as a basin for water flow and various kitchen tasks, such as washing dishes and food. The sink is located to the left of a wrench on the countertop and is partially visible to the immediate right of this countertop, where it contains various objects. This arrangement underscores the sink's role as a focal point in the kitchen, accommodating the practical needs of the space.</data>
