    <node id="Counter">
      <data key="d0">Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">furniture</data>
      <data key="d2">A counter is a flat surface commonly found in kitchens and bathrooms, utilized for various purposes including food preparation, storage, and other tasks. It serves as a versatile platform for placing items, making it an essential feature in both kitchens and other workspaces. Typically, counters are designed to facilitate tasks related to food preparation and enhance the functionality of these areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A";"can hold items;"provide workspace;provides workspace";support items"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The Counter is positioned flat in the kitchen setting, serving as a primary workspace for food-related activities.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Counter is a flat, horizontal surface that primarily serves as a workspace in kitchen and bathroom environments. It is a crucial element of kitchen setups, facilitating various activities such as food preparation, washing, and the placement of items. The Counter provides a designated area where utensils, food, and other cooking items can be organized and manipulated effectively. Often positioned above items like an orange cup, it underscores its functional role in supporting daily tasks. Overall, the Counter is an essential component that significantly aids in the efficiency and organization of both kitchens and bathrooms.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-2b703e57f7f312079f6c2ad3c93d259e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac88e7624d72a183b4aa96fb7a5fd8cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5577703269f1bf120829de56fbabfe5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7717aa9c0edd7bec036e22965a596b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-191e598f72ba5bb9098d142aa877c30b</data>
