    <node id="Kitchen Counter">
      <data key="d0">Kitchen Counter</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">"A flat surface used for food preparation and cooking"&lt;SEP&gt;"A flat surface used for various activities in a kitchen."&lt;SEP&gt;The Kitchen Counter is a fundamental flat working surface commonly found in kitchens, designed primarily for food preparation and various kitchen activities. It is characterized by a smooth, horizontal surface that facilitates the organization and management of cooking tasks, allowing for the placement of different kitchen objects. This particular kitchen counter features a dark gray countertop that spans the length of the kitchen along the back wall, complemented by white cabinets below with silver handles. The dark gray color not only supports food preparation but also enhances the overall aesthetic of the kitchen, making it a vital component of any home environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">"Can be used for assembling ingredients;"Can be used for placing items;"Can be used to place objects;"Can hold items;"Can hold various kitchen items;"N/A";"place items;"place objects;"surface for placing items;can hold tools and equipment";food preparation";part of the kitchen work area.";prepare food";preparing food";provide a working surface.";surface for food preparation"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A";"Should be kept clean to prevent contamination;may not support excessive weight without risk"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;"N/A"&lt;SEP&gt;The Kitchen Counter is centrally positioned within the kitchen, serving as a vital workspace. It occupies the lower part of the image and integrates with the walls and an adjoining sink. As the focal point of the kitchen, it holds multiple objects, including a pear, a hammer, a wrench, and a robotic arm, which are essential for various tasks. This arrangement enhances the efficiency of meal preparation, contributing to the overall functionality of the kitchen environment.</data>
      <data key="d7">The Kitchen Counter is a dark gray flat surface that is positioned horizontally across the background of the kitchen environment, occupying the lower part of the space and integrating seamlessly with the walls and adjoining sink. As a central feature of the kitchen, it serves multiple essential functions, acting as a versatile primary workspace designed to enhance efficiency in various culinary tasks. The counter facilitates practical applications in domestic settings and also serves as a social and interactive space, accommodating an array of kitchen items, including food, utensils, and tools.

Items may be organized along its surface for preparation and cooking, allowing for effective use during kitchen activities. The Kitchen Counter can host diverse objects such as a green apple-like item, a hammer, and even a robotic arm, highlighting its dynamic role in the kitchen. Overall, the Kitchen Counter is an integral component that supports organization and activity, making it a functional area where cooking, food preparation, and related tasks occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The kitchen counter serves as a workspace where various objects like food items and tools are arranged.&lt;SEP&gt;The kitchen counter serves as a workspace in the kitchen where various objects are placed and food is prepared.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-61e0642e7493eaadc2d0ef8540a842ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-842e2fbd96c01331a0e8b984f377b9eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b49dd2520a0dddbb4dcaa4dd60231f9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3110c2c46307410294a70a5f9d323898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43c0038cb33aa953ea92fe00f539c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91704b2974dfe887dc964702675320e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4bc8bccdf736abb2732024b3d6b6b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f47b87b4b95fbe187651b52c3814eca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d938391f0c5ac3146df4cf04a3a65025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60fb21a68457f79734302d0fad6e5d13</data>
