    </node>
    <node id="Task Goal">
      <data key="d0">Task Goal</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Task Goal represents a well-defined objective that guides an agent in navigating and observing its environment. It encompasses the specific aim of the task, which may include the movement of a designated item. Overall, the Task Goal serves to clarify the purpose and objectives that need to be achieved during the course of the task.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The Task Goal is defined as the intention behind the actions that an agent is expected to perform in the kitchen. It encompasses objectives related to various activities or operations within the environment, though these objectives may not always be explicitly outlined in the provided descriptions. In this particular scenario, the Task Goal includes the navigation to the refrigerator to observe its contents, indicating a focus on assessing available items. Additionally, it specifies an intent to move a pear item to a designated location, which is the sofa. Overall, the Task Goal encapsulates both the observation of the refrigerator's contents and the relocation of the pear, highlighting the agent's intended actions within the kitchen setting.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-42a8800fd5eb4780419dd640aa3c2edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512c99ba00abd1351acdffc5f28ef60b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d938391f0c5ac3146df4cf04a3a65025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6a9da891ede12376a00cfbf3a48e356</data>
