    <node id="Environment">
      <data key="d0">Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The environment refers to a surrounding condition in which objects exist or activities occur. It encompasses both tangible and abstract settings, characterized by visual elements that define the space. In a specific context, such as a kitchen, the term can denote the overall area where items are located and where various activities are carried out. Overall, the environment includes the surrounding conditions influencing the existence and interaction of objects and activities within a given space.</data>
      <data key="d3">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d4">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d5">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d6">"N/A"</data>
      <data key="d7">The environment refers to the context or surroundings that influence the presence and interaction of various objects. It is described both abstractly, highlighting the interplay of textures and colors that contribute to its composition, and specifically, as a kitchen setting that contains various items. This kitchen environment provides the context for the interaction of tools and food items, encompassing both the physical spaces and the overall framework within which these elements engage.</data>
      <data key="d8">chunk-ca4bc8bccdf736abb2732024b3d6b6b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f48f3a35cb5c6244f3f99abb6e97b4ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c58cfae8ce6565848740e41b83d48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77b7befda35befcb26d2d3f894305445</data>
      <data key="d9">unknown_source</data>
